            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a tasty, easy to make soup recipe. My husband loved it. The next time I make it however, I would reduce the amount of rice. The recipe calls for 2 cups and I only use 1 1/2 but still found that to be too much. Next time I will only use 1 cup of uncooked rice."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Karen D"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This soup is really great. I did one thing to alter it; we do not eat white rice in our home, so I used a wild rice blend from Wegman's supermarket. It really added to the heartiness of the soup.",
            "datePublished": "2006-03-18T07:30:32.280Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CaringCarp2393"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Read many reviews before starting the recipe AND used what I had on hand:) I always use extra garlic- especially in the winter, and lately I sub in my homemade, plain Greek yogurt for heavy cream. I also used ground spicy chicken sausage- had on hand- and keeper the smells coming by using my slow cooker! I served it with another Allrecipes post from long ago- homemade beer bread! Big hit with this meal on this cold, snowy, February day:)",
            "datePublished": "2025-02-16T19:33:33.939Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Heather I"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This had a good base. garlic, onions, chicken stock and the herbs and heavy cream. I changed alot though. I added chicken with the sausage, italian green beans and diced tomatoes for color and pasta (tortellini or ravioli would be good too). Then topped it with a blend of italian cheeses (parmesean cheese worked well too).\nMy husband loved it!",
            "datePublished": "2006-11-29T19:55:23.113Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "YellowFig4001"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Read the recipe people!! It calls for 2/3 cups of rice, not 2!! Very good with some minor changes. I added spinach and it was awesome.",
            "datePublished": "2025-02-16T22:47:22.884Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Chief"
            },
            "reviewBody": "A great soup and fairly simple to make. I heeded the advice of others who have made it, and used only one cup of rice instead of two. I thought it worked out perfectly. Additionally, I used a wild rice mix I had on hand instead of plain white rice. Finally, I threw in some leftover chicken breast I had in the fridge along with the sausage. All in all, I thought it was an excellent soup and will be making it again very soon.",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-28T01:05:46.870Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "FriskyCane2487"
            },
            "reviewBody": "A little salty! Less chicken broth next time. I skipped step 2 and it was still great. I used some Trader Joe’s chicken sausages. I subbed heavy cream for 1/2cup oat milk and 1tbspn corn starch for my lactose intolerant husband.",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-16T22:35:26.274Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Karen H."
            },
            "reviewBody": "If you like a thick hearty soup, you will like this recipe. Once the rice was almost cooked, I added another 2 cups of chicken stock and it was still very thick. If you want any broth at all in the soup, I recommend using a cup or less of rice. It also needed more flavor so I topped each bowl with fresh basil, cracked pepper and a little Parmesan cheese, which helped.",
            "datePublished": "2025-01-20T20:02:38.601Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SB Bronx, NY"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Used 6 cups of stock, not eight. Took sausage out of casing, meat was more tender.",
            "datePublished": "2025-04-03T18:07:12.150Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
