            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "PeppyPot1742"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I use a pound of bulk hot Italian sausage in place of links and just crumbled it and cooked it as you would with links. It turned out well.",
            "datePublished": "2025-02-23T19:34:31.703Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Juliehm"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious and simple. Cut back on simmer time before and after adding the rice. Used a combination of orzo and rice due to what I had on hand. Adjusted Italian seasoning per our taste. Served with focaccia. Will definitely make again!",
            "datePublished": "2025-02-19T11:28:24.276Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Keenan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Simple and effective! This is as simple as it gets, but the results are still top quality. I turned it into a Paella-like dish by using unwashed white rice (to keep the extra starch) and doubling every aspect of the recipe except the chicken broth. I was prepared to add water to fill as necessary, but it worked perfectly without! It could've been a Risotto if I had some good white cheese to add at the end. The one modification I'd make next time, is that I'd cook the sausages first to *properly* brown them, remove them from the pan, and then brown the onion and garlic in the sausage grease before re-adding the sausage with the rice and broth.",
            "datePublished": "2025-12-24T06:07:53.074Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BlueMiso5463"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very reminiscent of an Italian Wedding type soup but richer. We used 1 chopped medium onion and 4 cloves of garlic. Fresh butcher made Italian sweet sausage is a must. Hot sausage might be an interesting change. Next time we'll increase the rice to at least a cup and finish with a good imported grated cheese.",
            "datePublished": "2025-02-24T00:46:20.567Z"
          },
